@@ -2,4 +2,39 @@
 
 Reservations of capacity for the nodes of a tenant tree.
 
+## Usage
+
+`Pool(tree, quotas)` builds a pool over a tenant tree. `tree` maps each node to
+its parent, and the root to `None`. `quotas` maps every node of the tree to an
+integer quota of at least 0.
+
+```python
+from pool import NoCapacity, Pool
+
+pool = Pool({"root": None, "team": "root"}, {"root": 10, "team": 6})
+rid = pool.reserve("team", 4, 0, 5)
+```
+
+`reserve` returns an integer id. A reservation holds `units` of capacity at its
+node for the instants `t` with `start <= t < end`, and it must fit under the
+quota of every node in the chain from its own node up to the root. A request
+that fits becomes active. With `wait=True`, a request that does not fit becomes
+waiting and keeps its place in line. With `preempt=True`, a request that does
+not fit may displace active reservations of a strictly lower priority.
+
+`usage(node, at)` is the capacity used by the active reservations in the
+subtree of `node` at instant `at`. `peak(node, start, end)` is the highest usage
+at an instant in `[start, end)`, and `timeline(node)` lists the `(instant,
+usage)` pairs at which the usage of the node changes. `waiting()` lists the ids
+of the waiting reservations in waiting order, and `cancel(rid)` cancels an
+active or waiting reservation.
+
+`set_quota(node, quota, evict=True)` lowers a quota, evicting active
+reservations as needed. Without `evict=True`, a quota that the current usage is
+above raises `ValueError`. `events()` returns the events appended so far, in
+order, as a new list.
+
+A request that cannot be placed raises `NoCapacity`; its `node` and `at`
+attributes name the first violation.
+
 `pool/steps.py` is maintained by the timeline slice.
